UID: SLICE-SEMANTIC-LAYER-RENDER
TITLE: Render the semantic layer as an HTML artifact to judge from, not as text
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Render the semantic layer as an HTML artifact the operator can read on a phone
and judge from, instead of as linear text. Read as WORK under
DEC-SLICE-DECOMPOSES-TO-WORK.

THE INPUT is MECH-SEMANTIC-LAYER-WHITEBOARD (the tagged one-sheet), the
collapsed vocabulary (REQUIREMENT, USE CASE, MECHANISM, EVIDENCE, DECISION,
NARRATIVE, WORK -- never the dissolved names), and the nodes it cites. Nothing
in it is settled; the render shows what was EXPLORED so the operator can
decide what to settle.

WHAT THE RENDER MUST DO, learned by failing three times on 2026-08-29:

- A graph cannot be read as a flat list. Each attempt to linearize the sheet
  got denser, not clearer, and on a phone node names and field names landed
  in one column with nothing to tell them apart. Render structure as
  structure: one screen per node type, fields separate from edges, edges as a
  diagram, status as colour with a legend.
- Show one thing at a time. The operator reads a node plus its neighbours
  (docs/sdoc/render.py --uid is the precedent), never the whole canon.
  Navigation between screens, not scrolling through everything.
- No coined terms. Only the ruled glossary and plain words; every UID shown
  with its title.
- The five top gaps from the whiteboard's last section get their own screen,
  each with the nodes it touches linked.
- Then decisions come as cards, one per turn, AFTER the operator has read
  the render -- not before, and not inside it.

THE TOOL is the harness's HTML artifact (a private rendered page). Build it
as a self-contained page, mobile-first, theme-aware. Do not present the
semantic layer in chat text again.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Filed 2026-08-29 after three failed text presentations in one session. The
operator's words: 'we aren't aligned on what it means to generate something for
human consumption'. The next session starts here, via docs/sdoc/README.md.

DELIVERED 2026-08-29 (session 7), private artifact:
https://claude.ai/code/artifact/9cdae156-301a-4baa-8d20-585dd6125d4e

Shape: a Start screen (colour legend, a per-topic bar of the five tags, the
node-type grid, the four layers, the five top gaps); one screen per ruled type
with fields, state ladders and relations shown separately; an Edges screen
with a diagram of every live (source, role, target) combination and the
fingerprint pairs; thirteen topic screens with a plain-language headline per
line and the sheet's own wording one tap below; five gap screens with the nodes
each touches and the lines that feed it; a screen per cited node with its
neighbours; a Words screen. Every UID is shown with its title. Nothing is
presented as settled.

Measured: 145 tagged lines plus the five top gaps; the sheet's tag counts
reproduce exactly from the parse; 59 UIDs cited, 95 nodes on the page with
one-hop neighbours; every cited UID resolved against the export at bbcc0060.
The five tag colours pass the colour-vision validator in both themes.

Reviewed before hand-over by five independent readers (three for headline
fidelity, one for vocabulary, one mechanical) with contested findings argued
both ways: 37 raised, 23 confirmed and fixed, 6 split (resolved by falling
back to the sheet's own wording; listed in the hand-over for the operator to
overrule), 4 refuted, 4 nits fixed. Screenshot passes at phone and desktop
width caught three layout defects before review.

The generator is not in the repository: MECH-RENDER-GENERATOR-OUTSIDE-REPO.
<<<
